[21.126471, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1mGenerated Queries:\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[36m==================\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m1\u001b[39m\u001b[0m. \u001b[2m[order: 1, merge: true]\u001b[0m \u001b[1m\u001b[92mrfx\u001b[39m\u001b[0m \u001b[97mquery \"trigram\" --paths\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[92mFound\u001b[39m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m\u001b[97m50\u001b[39m\u001b[0m \u001b[2mtotal results across\u001b[0m \u001b[1m\u001b[97m50\u001b[39m\u001b[0m \u001b[2mfiles:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mCHANGELOG.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m7\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m7\u001b[39m: - `trigrams.bin` V4 and `content.bin` V2 — **re-index required**. A V3 index is served from an in-memory rebuild (slow) until `rfx index` runs; `rfx index` detects the schema change and rebuilds in full. Postings are now one per distinct trigram per line, grouped into per-file blocks, with no byte offsets: 3.9x → 0.9x of corpus size on the synthetic latency corpus (127 MB → 30 MB), 1.4x on the Reflex repo. `TrigramIndex::load` is O(files) — the directory is binary-searched in the mmap instead of b…\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mCLAUDE.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m6\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m6\u001b[39m: Reflex uses **trigram-based indexing** to enable instant full-text search across large codebases (10k+ files). Unlike symbol-only tools, Reflex finds **every occurrence** of patterns—function calls, variable usage, comments, and more—not just definitions. Results include file paths, line numbers, and surrounding context, with optional symbol-aware filtering.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mCONTRIBUTING.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m9\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m9\u001b[39m: 1. **Speed**: Extremely fast queries on large codebases through efficient trigram indexing\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mREADME.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m178\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m178\u001b[39m: # Case-insensitive (like rg -i); still uses the trigram index\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/ref225-phase2-analysis.py\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m41\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m41\u001b[39m:     \"reflex-comp-trigram-extract\",   # 4.0 (marginal)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/ref225-validity-gate.py\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m33\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m33\u001b[39m:     \"reflex-comp-query-path\", \"reflex-comp-trigram-extract\", \"reflex-comp-deleted-file\",\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/repos.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m20\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m20\u001b[39m: | `ripgrep` | `BurntSushi/ripgrep`    | `14.1.1`       | `4649aa9700619f94cf9c66876e9549d83420e16c` | Rust, small/medium, well-understood multi-crate workspace; trigram-friendly. |\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/run-ref225-arm-a.sh\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m44\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m44\u001b[39m:   \"reflex-comp-trigram-extract\"\r\n\r\n"]
[21.126516, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/run-ref225-phase2.sh\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m74\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m74\u001b[39m:   \"reflex-comp-trigram-extract\"\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/runner.py\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m249\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m249\u001b[39m:     \"\"\"Build the rfx trigram index in repo_dir if it is absent.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/tasks/SCHEMA.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m97\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m97\u001b[39m:   file: src/trigram.rs\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/tasks/iteration-forcing.yaml\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m65\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m65\u001b[39m:   - id: reflex-comp-trigram-extract\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/efficacy/tasks/reflex.yaml\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m25\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m25\u001b[39m:       file: src/trigram.rs\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbenches/trigram_bench.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m1\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m1\u001b[39m: //! Criterion benchmarks for the trigram indexing and query pipeline.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mbuild.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m15\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m15\u001b[39m: //! - src/trigram.rs: Inverted index format for trigrams.bin (posting lists)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mdocs/ARCHITECTURE.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m26\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m26\u001b[39m: Reflex is a **trigram-based full-text code search engine** with optional symbol-aware filtering. The architecture prioritizes:\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mdocs/DEPENDENCIES.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m616\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m616\u001b[39m: Base query: 2-5ms (trigram search)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96mdocs/mcp-tool-cheatsheet.md\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m179\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m179\u001b[39m: | `ignore_case` | bool | `true` = `rg -i` (with `contains`: `rg -i -F`). On `search_code`, `search_regex`, `count_occurrences`, `list_locations`, `find_references`. Uses the trigram index, so it costs about the same as a case-sensitive search |\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/ast_query.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m15\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m15\u001b[39m: //! - Requires trigram pre-filtering (no AST-only queries allowed)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/atomic_write.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m103\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m103\u001b[39m:         // Partial trigram batches of an indexer that died between two batches.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/cli/misc.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m30\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m30\u001b[39m:     // Read trigram count from trigrams.bin header (magic + version + num_trigrams + num_files = 24 bytes)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/cli/mod.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m148\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m148\u001b[39m:         /// WARNING: AST queries bypass trigram optimization and scan the entire codebase.\r\n"]
[21.126535, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/content_store.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m5\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m5\u001b[39m: //! - Verifying trigram matches\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/indexer.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m55\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m55\u001b[39m:     /// The file's trigram postings, extracted in the pool (no file id yet).\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/lib.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[21.126542, "o", "  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m10\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m10\u001b[39m: //! - **Indexer**: Scans code and builds trigram index; writes to cache\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/mcp.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m284\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m284\u001b[39m:                             \"description\": \"Match letters regardless of case, like `rg -i` (`ignore_case` + `contains` is `rg -i -F`). Default false. The trigram index is still used, so this costs about the same as a case-sensitive search.\"\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/models.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m541\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m541\u001b[39m:     /// Maximum entries per trigram posting list (0 = unlimited).\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/parsers/mod.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[21.126555, "o", "  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m113\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m113\u001b[39m:                  trigram-indexed only and has no grammar. Use full-text or regex \\\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/pulse/wiki.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m1430\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m1430\u001b[39m:     // Count references for priority-kind symbols only via the trigram index.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/query/filter.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m44\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m44\u001b[39m:     /// search is a plain trigram scan and would otherwise return the name in a\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/query/mod.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m58\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m58\u001b[39m:     /// Time spent in trigram lookup and intersection.\r\n\r\n"]
[21.126566, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/query/open_index.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m4\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m4\u001b[39m: //! (three to four times per query, once per phase), parsed the whole trigram\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/query/result.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m1\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m1\u001b[39m: //! Result assembly utilities: trigram index reconstruction and file-id resolution\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[96msrc/regex_trigrams.rs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2mLine\u001b[0m \u001b[93m1\u001b[39m-\u001b[93m1\u001b[39m: //! Extract literal sequences from regex patterns for trigram optimization\r\n\r\n"]
